      "id": 1,
      "text": "Allyn was named after Judge Frank Allyn of Tacoma, whose influence helped shape the town when it was platted in 1889.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allyn%2C_Washington",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first settlers arrived in 1853, establishing the roots of what would become Allyn.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allyn%2C_Washington",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "From the 1870s to the 1920s, steamboats ferried passengers and goods between Allyn and neighboring communities along Case Inlet.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allyn%2C_Washington",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The final steamboat voyage from Tacoma to Allyn ran in 1924, marking the end of an era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allyn%2C_Washington",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Lakeland Village surrounds a 27‑hole golf course and a 50‑acre private lake, Lake Anderson, offering residents year‑round recreation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
